 "text": "Hi, how's everything with you? Pick a spot in the middle of the smallest area, away from trees and trees. A flat spot is ideal, and take down any branches. That' a classic camp ground spot. Just make sure the tree isn't going fall on you. Look up at night and check it' not leaning. That's fine, as long as it not rotting into the ground. Push it gently with your foot, it should give way a bit. Avoid the area around the fire pit, it's often a narrow strip with trees. Pick a spot in flattest bit and keep it short. That's the idea. Just tie the tent in at the door and use the guy ropes if the wind picks up.",
